    tmk:spanEnd 457 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "The trade mark application may be accepted if the applicant provides a Letter of Consent from the PBR title holder, agreeing to the use and registration of the PBR variety name or synonym as part of a trade mark for the offending goods (see s 11 of the PBR Act). In this circumstance, the owner of the trade mark will need to agree to an endorsement to that effect. The goods will also need to be restricted to accord with the plant variety name or synonym." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

