    tmk:spanEnd 1118 ;
    tmk:spanStart 879 ;
    tmk:supportingText "In cases such as these, the trade marks are, to some extent, inherently adapted to distinguish, but the extent of adaptation is low and is therefore not sufficient for the trade marks to be accepted without evidence or other circumstances." ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

