tmkc:GC-0062 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:GroundOfRefusal,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "One of the two limbs of section 42; the Manual's Part 30 pairs it with use contrary to law but the Act keeps them as separate paragraphs, and only this one is about the mark's content rather than the consequences of using it."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "scandalous sign"@en-AU,
        "scandalous signs"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "scandalous matter"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Both the Act and the Manual state the ground in one sentence. Held apart from 'use contrary to law' because paragraph 42(a) looks at what the mark contains and paragraph 42(b) at what using it would do — different evidence answers each."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/1%231>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/2%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the preferred label should be the Act's 'scandalous matter' or the Manual's heading 'scandalous signs'. The Act's phrase is narrower — matter within a sign — and this record follows the Act."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0062" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s42(a)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "prescribed sign"@en-AU,
        "prohibited sign"@en-AU,
        "use contrary to law"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s42>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/2%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0062 .

tmkc:GC-0072 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:SubjectMatter ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual makes the point that matters most here: the definition of trade mark is closed and exhaustive, while the definition of sign is open and inclusive. A sign is a trade mark only when used or intended to be used to distinguish in the course of trade."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "mark"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 17 defines it in terms and the Manual explains the character of the definition. Held apart from 'sign' because the Manual says in one sentence why they are not the same kind of definition."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/1%231>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/3%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'mark' is really an alt_label. The Manual uses it as the 1955 Act's word and the 1995 Act deliberately replaced it, which may make it historical rather than current."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0072" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s17>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/trade-mark> ;
    tmk:notLabel "business name"@en-AU,
        "registered trade mark"@en-AU,
        "sign"@en-AU,
        "trade name"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s17>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/3%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0072 .

tmkc:GC-0077 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:SubjectMatter ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual's test is functional rather than formal: whatever the sound is, it must serve the purpose of identifying the trade source."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "auditory trade mark"@en-AU,
        "sound (auditory) trade marks"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "sound trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual opens its section on sound marks with the definition and closes the paragraph with the functional requirement."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part21/6%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the Manual's 'sensory trade marks' heading should be a broader concept over sound and scent."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0077" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/sign> ;
    tmk:notLabel "scent trade mark"@en-AU,
        "sign"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part21/6%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0077 .

tmkc:GC-0085 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "Load-bearing in two places at once: section 41(5) makes a predecessor's use count as the applicant's for distinctiveness, and section 44(4) does the same for prior use. The section 6 definition itself is a stub that continues into a list."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "predecessor in title"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Act states the consequence in terms in section 41(5); the section 6 definition is a stub whose text does not carry the substance, so the evidence is drawn from the operative provision instead."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/6%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the concept should carry the section 6 list as narrower concepts. The stub continues into subparagraphs this record does not reach."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0085" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(5)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44(4)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/predecessor-in-title> ;
    tmk:notLabel "assignment"@en-AU,
        "authorised user"@en-AU,
        "registered owner"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0085 .

tmkc:GC-0099 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:InstrumentOrRecord,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual defines it as a limitation of the exclusive rights given by registration, and explains that the owner never had exclusive rights in part of a mark anyway — so a disclaimer records something rather than creating it."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "disclaimers"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "disclaimer"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined in terms by the Manual with the statutory reference attached."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part24/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether a disclaimer is a species of the section 6 'limitations' or a different instrument. The Manual's wording supports the first; the Act's structure the second."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0099" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s74>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s74(1)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "conditions or limitations"@en-AU,
        "endorsement"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part24/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0099 .

tmkc:GC-0116 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProcessRole ;
    rdfs:comment "Defined by the Act as the person in whose name the application currently stands — so the applicant can change without the application changing. The Manual's Part 10 treats getting the identity right as a formality requirement in its own right."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "applicant"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined in terms, and the 'for the time being' clause is the part worth keeping — it is what makes assignment of a pending application coherent."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the definition source should be Part 10.1 on the name requirement or a passage about who may apply under section 27."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0116" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s27>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/applicant> ;
    tmk:notLabel "authorised user"@en-AU,
        "opponent"@en-AU,
        "registered owner"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/applicant> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0116 .

tmkc:GC-0118 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual is careful here and the record follows it: the expression does not appear in the Act. It is a reading of section 33's structure, endorsed by Branson J in Blount, that the Registrar must accept unless satisfied of a ground. GC-0007 already holds this term."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "presumption that a trade mark is registrable"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "presumption of registrability"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Two passages, and they are in mild tension — Part 20.4 asserts the presumption and Part 22.2 says the expression is not in the Act. Both are quoted rather than reconciled, because the tension is the interesting part and resolving it would be authoring a position the corpus does not take."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/2%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the two passages really are in tension or whether Part 22.2 is only saying the phrase is not a statutory term. The record takes the second reading and quotes both."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0118" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33(1)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "acceptance"@en-AU,
        "ground for rejection"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/2%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0118 .

tmkc:GC-0125 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "Examination of Class 31 plant applications takes in the Plant Breeder's Rights Act 1994 — legislation outside the Trade Marks Act entirely. That is the interesting thing about this concept and the reason it is held."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "plant varietal names"@en-AU,
        "plant variety denomination"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "plant varietal name"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states the interaction in terms. Held because it is one of two places where examination reaches outside the trade marks legislation, and a vocabulary built only from the Act would never find it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32A/1/1/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32A/1/1/2> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The legislative_basis. This record names s 41 and s 43 as the grounds the varietal name bears on, which is an inference from Part 22.27's title rather than a citation in the quoted passage."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0125" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s43> ;
    tmk:notLabel "generic term"@en-AU,
        "geographical indication"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32A/1/1/1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0125 .

tmkc:GC-0126 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "The second place examination reaches outside the trade marks legislation: the Wine Australia Act 2013. Distinguished from the section 6 'geographical indication' because the protection comes from a different statute."@en-AU ;
