    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Regulations expressly define the term, making it a distinct legal concept best classified as a registration record. It is broader than GC-0113, international registration designating Australia, because its definition does not require an Australian designation. The Manual also distinguishes international registration from Australian protection by describing the effect of cancellation on a protected international trade mark. The defining legislative passage is regulation 17A.2. The only reference supplied under PROVISIONS, regulation 17A.27, is described in the Manual as defining a declaration period for limitations, so it is not listed as a legislative basis for this concept."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.7e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2/international-registration> ;
