tmkc:GC-0113 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:SubjectMatter ;
    rdfs:comment "The Australian half of a Madrid registration. It is examined much as a domestic application is, which is why the Manual's Parts 26 to 31 keep referring to it, and it becomes a protected international trade mark rather than a registered trade mark."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "IRDA"@en-AU,
        "international registration designating Australia (IRDA)"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "international registration designating Australia"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Regulations define the term by pointing at another regulation whose text this record does not quote, so the basis is inferred rather than explicit. It is held because 86 Manual passages use the abbreviation and the vocabulary could not read them."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 6e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/1/1/1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The evidence. This record's statutory citation is a pointer, not a definition, and the definition it points at should replace it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0113" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r2.1/irda> ;
    tmk:notLabel "international registration"@en-AU,
        "protected international trade mark"@en-AU,
        "trade mark application"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/1/1/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r2.1/irda> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0113 .

tmkc:GC-0127 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:InstrumentOrRecord,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual's Part 52 opens by listing what gets decided — oppositions to registration, to removal for non-use, to procedural matters — and section 205 makes a Deputy Registrar's decision the Registrar's."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "Registrar's decision"@en-AU,
        "written decision"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "decision"@en-AU ;
    skos:related tmkc:GC-0040,
        tmkc:GC-0128 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The evidence is a list of what is decided rather than a definition of a decision, which is the weakest kind of support in this pass. The concept is held anyway because 178 Manual passages use the word and a knowledge base about examination that cannot say 'decision' is missing something structural."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 6e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/1%231~1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "This record's evidence does not define a decision. Either Part 52 defines it somewhere this pass did not reach, or the record should be redrawn or dropped."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0127" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s205>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s35> ;
    tmk:notLabel "adverse report"@en-AU,
        "ground for rejection"@en-AU,
        "hearing"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/1%231~1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0127 .

tmkc:GC-0130 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "Does different work in different places: it is what a defensive registration rests on, and it is the basis of the section 60 opposition ground. GC-0050 already holds this term from the section 43 pilot."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "reputation in Australia"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "reputation"@en-AU ;
    tmk:allocatesTo tmkc:GC-0117 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The evidence is the defensive-registration requirement, which is reputation described rather than named. Held because reputation is one of the few concepts that genuinely spans the Manual — Parts 29, 34, 46 and 47 all reason with it — and the boundary removal is what makes that visible. Overlaps the signed GC-0050."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 6e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/1/1/1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether reputation under section 43, section 60 and section 185 is one concept or three. This is the most consequential unresolved question in the pass."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0130" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s185>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s60> ;
    tmk:notLabel "connotation"@en-AU,
        "evidence of use"@en-AU,
        "use of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
