tmkc:GC-0060 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:LegalTest ;
    rdfs:comment "The first half of the Manual's two-part inherent-adaptation process. It is assessed 'in the light of the applied for goods and/or services', so it is not the word's meaning in the abstract."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "ordinary signification of the trade mark"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "ordinary signification"@en-AU ;
    tmk:appliesTo tmkc:GC-0073 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual names it as the first step of a two-part process and ties it to the goods and services applied for. It is held apart from 'connotation' — a section 43 concept this repository already holds — because the two ask different questions of the same mark and share no statutory text."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/3%231~1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The relationship to connotation. An expert may see them as two names for one underlying idea applied under different sections, which would make this a 'related' rather than a distinct concept."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0060" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(3)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(4)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "connotation"@en-AU,
        "denotation"@en-AU,
        "dictionary meaning"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:qualifies tmkc:GC-0061,
        tmkc:GC-0119 ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/3%231~1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0060 .

tmkc:GC-0061 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:LegalTest ;
    rdfs:comment "The second half of the two-part process. The label is this repository's, not the Manual's — the Manual states the idea in a clause rather than naming it — and that is the most likely thing to be wrong about this record."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "other traders might legitimately wish to use"@en-AU,
        "the need of other traders"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "other traders' legitimate desire to use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The corpus states the idea in terms but gives it no name, so the record is corpus_explicit as to the content and an invention as to the label. It is held because an examiner reasons with it constantly and a vocabulary without it cannot represent the second half of the Manual's own method."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 6e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/3%231~1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The preferred label, which no passage supports. The case law phrase is closer to 'the legitimate desire of other traders', and an expert should replace this label rather than accept it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0061" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(3)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(4)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "honest concurrent use"@en-AU,
        "ordinary signification"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:qualifies tmkc:GC-0120 ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/3%231~1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0061 .

tmkc:GC-0079 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:SubjectMatter ;
    rdfs:comment "A single application for two or more marks that resemble each other in material particulars and differ only in the ways section 51 lists. The 'material particulars' requirement is what does the work and the Manual gives it its own numbered section."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "series"@en-AU,
        "series application"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "series of trade marks"@en-AU ;
    skos:related tmkc:GC-0111 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Both the Act and the Manual state it in terms."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part13/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the allowable differences in section 51(1)(a)–(c) should be narrower concepts. The Manual gives them their own section."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extendsTo tmkc:GC-0074 ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0079" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51(1)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "composite trade mark"@en-AU,
        "divisional application"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:requiresElement tmkc:GC-0080 ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part13/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0079 .

tmkc:GC-0081 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual calls use a concept fundamental to trade mark law and lists the questions it bears on: capability to distinguish, honest concurrent or prior use, ownership. Section 6 says its meaning is 'affected by' subsections 7(1), (2) and (3) — which is not the same as being defined by them."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "trade mark use"@en-AU,
        "use"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "use of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
    skos:related tmkc:GC-0104 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states the concept's place in the scheme and the Act tells us where its meaning is affected. Held as one concept with the specialised uses — authorised, prior, honest concurrent — as separate records beside it, because each answers a different question under a different provision."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19A/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'use in the course of trade' should be the preferred label. Section 17 makes the course of trade part of what a trade mark is, and the bare word 'use' may be too wide for a vocabulary that also holds authorised use and prior use."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0081" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s17>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/use-of-a-trade-mark>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s7> ;
    tmk:notLabel "authorised use"@en-AU,
        "evidence of use"@en-AU,
        "honest concurrent use"@en-AU,
        "prior use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/use-of-a-trade-mark>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19A/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0081 .

tmkc:GC-0090 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "Section 44 turns on a comparison of priority dates, and a convention claim can move one. Distinct from the filing date, which section 6 defines separately, though for many applications the two coincide. GC-0016 already holds this term from the section 43 pilot."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "priority date"@en-AU ;
    skos:related tmkc:GC-0122 ;
    tmk:appliesTo tmkc:GC-0110,
        tmkc:GC-0111,
        tmkc:GC-0114 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined by section 12 and pointed to by section 6. Written from the statute rather than from Part 29, which is what GC-0016 rests on; the overlap is flagged rather than resolved."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part11/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The overlap with the signed GC-0016. One of the two should be retired by a reviewer, and an agent may not choose which."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0090" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s12>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/priority-date> ;
    tmk:notLabel "date of registration"@en-AU,
        "filing date"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:qualifies tmkc:GC-0064 ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s12>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/priority-date> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0090 .

tmkc:GC-0106 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProceduralStep ;
    rdfs:comment "Renewable indefinitely at ten-year intervals from the filing date, and — unusually — any person may effect it, not only the owner."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "renewal"@en-AU ;
