    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states who an opponent generally is. The statutory definitions differ by proceeding and are deliberately not merged here (CLAUDE.md rule 6)."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part46/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the six statutory definitions of 'opponent' are the same concept. The candidate pass found them and refused to choose; this record inherits that refusal."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0117" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/opponent>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r5.2> ;
    tmk:notLabel "applicant"@en-AU,
        "objector"@en-AU,
        "requester"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part46/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0117 .

tmkc:GC-0119 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:LegalTest ;
    rdfs:comment "The first of the Manual's three categories. A mark is here if it has no ordinary signification for the goods, or has one that other traders are not likely to want without improper motive."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "prima facie capable"@en-AU,
        "sufficiently inherently adapted to distinguish"@en-AU ;
    skos:broader tmkc:GC-0058 ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "prima facie capable of distinguishing"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states the rule for the category in terms. Held separately because the three-category sort is how Part 22 organises everything after it, and a vocabulary without the categories cannot follow the argument."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/4%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the three categories should be one concept with three values rather than three concepts. This pass holds two of the three and that asymmetry is itself a defect."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0119" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(2)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(3)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(4)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "capable of distinguishing"@en-AU,
        "inherent adaptation to distinguish"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/4%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0119 .

tmkc:GC-0120 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:LegalTest ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual's third category and the hardest to overcome: only use before the filing date sufficient to make the mark in fact distinguish will do it. The Manual's list of examples — pictorial representations, geographical names, laudatory words — is the practical content of the category."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "not to any extent inherently adapted to distinguish"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "no inherent adaptation to distinguish"@en-AU ;
    skos:related tmkc:GC-0059 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states the category and exemplifies it in one sentence. Held for the same reason as the first category."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/6%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The missing middle category — limited inherent adaptation but not prima facie capable, the Manual's Part 22.5. This pass holds the outer two and not the middle, which is an omission rather than a judgement."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0120" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(3)(a)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "inherent adaptation to distinguish"@en-AU,
        "prima facie capable of distinguishing"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:requiresElement tmkc:GC-0058,
        tmkc:GC-0101 ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/6%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0120 .

tmkc:GC-0129 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:InstrumentOrRecord,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "What the applicant claims, as against how it is classified and whether it is similar to something else. Amending it is one of the Manual's named ways of overcoming a section 44 ground. GC-0012 already holds this term."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "specification"@en-AU,
        "specification of goods and/or services"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "specification of goods and services"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The evidence states what a specification is for in the one place it does operative work in examination. That is thinner than a definition and is flagged. Overlaps the signed GC-0012."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 6.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/5%231> ;
    tmk:dependsOnExternalSource tmkc:GC-0121 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Both the overlap with GC-0012 and the evidence, which is drawn from Part 27 rather than from the Part 10 section this record cites as its definition source."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0129" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s27(1)(b)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r4.4> ;
    tmk:notLabel "classification of goods and services"@en-AU,
        "similarity of goods and services"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:qualifies tmkc:GC-0014,
        tmkc:GC-0033 ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0129 .

tmkc:GC-0013 a tmk:Exception ;
    skos:broader tmkc:GC-0069 ;
    skos:related tmkc:GC-0022,
        tmkc:GC-0129 ;
    tmk:appliesTo tmkc:GC-0018 ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0013 .

tmkc:GC-0056 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:LegalTest ;
    rdfs:comment "A resemblance test that is not the section 44 one. The comparison is between the applicant's sign and a prescribed or prohibited sign, and the threshold is 'likely to be taken for it' rather than 'likely to deceive or cause confusion'."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "so nearly resembling as to be likely to be taken for it"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "so nearly resembling"@en-AU ;
    tmk:appliesTo tmkc:GC-0073 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The phrase is the Act's and the Manual quotes it as the operative test for subparagraph 39(2)(b)(i). It is held as a separate concept from deceptive similarity because the two use different words for different comparisons, and collapsing them would let a section 44 authority be cited into a section 39 question."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/2%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether practice in fact applies the section 10 case law to this test. If it does, the two concepts are more closely related than this record says."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0056" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s39(2)(b)> ;
    tmk:mayGiveRiseTo tmkc:GC-0063 ;
    tmk:notLabel "deceptively similar"@en-AU,
        "substantially identical"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s39>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/2%231> ;
    tmk:statesThresholdFor tmkc:GC-0006,
        tmkc:GC-0053 ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0056 .

tmkc:GC-0093 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProceduralStep ;
    rdfs:comment "Section 33(1) makes acceptance mandatory unless the Registrar is satisfied of a defect or a ground — that is the presumption of registrability in operation. Acceptance is not registration: section 33 accepts, publication and opposition follow, and registration comes later."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "accept the application"@en-AU,
        "accepted"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "acceptance"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Both the Act and the Manual state it in terms, and the Manual explicitly ties it to the presumption of registrability."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Nothing specific."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0093" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33(1)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33(2)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "deferment of acceptance"@en-AU,
        "registration"@en-AU,
        "revocation of acceptance"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0093 .

tmkc:GC-0102 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProceduralStep ;
    rdfs:comment "A formal objection by a third party. The Manual notes that any person may oppose but that the opponent is generally somebody affected — which is a practice observation rather than a standing requirement, and the record keeps it in notes for that reason."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "opposition proceedings"@en-AU,
        "opposition to registration"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "opposition"@en-AU ;
    tmk:appliesTo tmkc:GC-0113 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined in terms at the head of the Manual's Part on the subject."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part46/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'any person may oppose' should be in the record rather than the notes. It is a statement about standing and belongs in a relationship record if anywhere."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0102" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s52>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r5.2> ;
    tmk:mayGiveRiseTo tmkc:GC-0114 ;
    tmk:notLabel "hearing"@en-AU,
        "rectification"@en-AU,
        "removal for non-use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part46/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0102 .

tmkc:GC-0114 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:SubjectMatter ;
    rdfs:comment "The Madrid equivalent of a registered trade mark, and section 44's note 4 makes it citable against a domestic application. Holding it apart from 'registered trade mark' is what lets a citation search reach both."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "protected international trade mark designating Australia"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "protected international trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 44's note names the term and states its effect on examination, which is the operative fact. The Regulations' own definition is a pointer, as with IRDA."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/1/1/1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The definition source is a Part 60 passage about the Protocol generally rather than about protection specifically."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0114" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r2.1/protected-international-trade-mark> ;
    tmk:notLabel "IRDA"@en-AU,
        "international registration"@en-AU,
        "registered trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0114 .

tmkc:GC-0046 a tmk:ProcessRole ;
    skos:related tmkc:GC-0040,
        tmkc:GC-0041,
